<Legal
  title="Refunds"
  description="Fourteen days, no questions asked, on any Bubo Pro key. Paddle handles the money as merchant of record."
  path="/refund"
  updated="30 July 2026"
>
  <h1>Refunds</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Fourteen days from the day you buy, no questions asked. Email
    <a href="mailto:support@weekndlabs.com">support@weekndlabs.com</a> and say you
    want a refund. You do not have to give a reason, and we will not ask for one.
  </p>

  <h2>What happens</h2>
  <p>
    Bubo Pro is sold through Paddle, who are the merchant of record. That means
    Paddle takes the payment, handles the tax, and issues the refund back to the
    card or account you paid with. We tell them to refund; they move the money.
    How long it takes to appear on your statement is your bank's business, and
    it is usually a few working days.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your license key stops being valid when the refund goes through, and Bubo
    goes back to Personal. Personal is free and stays free, so the app keeps
    working.
  </p>

  <h2>After fourteen days</h2>
  <p>
    Write to us anyway. If Bubo is broken on your Mac and we cannot fix it, we
    would rather give you your money back than keep it. Paddle can also refund
    on its own terms as the seller of record, whatever this page says.
  </p>

  <h2>Before you buy</h2>
  <p>
    Bubo is free to download and use on the Personal plan, with no account and
    no time limit. Pro adds a license key for up to three of your own Macs and
    updates for this major version. Try Personal first if you are unsure: it
    costs nothing and it is the same app.
  </p>
</Legal>
